# ============================================================================
# PARADA Mobile environment
#
# IMPORTANT:
#   - EXPO_PUBLIC_* values are PUBLIC client configuration. Never put secrets
#     (CAMERA_API_KEY, JWT secrets, DB credentials) in these variables.
#   - Copy this file to `.env` within apps/mobile and fill in your values.
#   - `.env` is gitignored (see repository root .gitignore).
# ============================================================================

# Base URL of the PARADA backend API.
#   - iOS Simulator / web:   http://localhost:4100
#   - Android Emulator:      http://10.0.2.2:4100
#   - Physical device:       http://<your-LAN-IP>:4100  (the phone's localhost
#                            is the phone itself, NOT your dev machine)
EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.1.100:4100

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Expo / Metro on a multi-homed Windows host
#
# Metro runs on port 8082 (see package.json), not Expo's default 8081: on this
# development machine port 8081 is already claimed by the Windows Host Network
# Service (hns — Docker Desktop / WSL2 port proxying), which accepts the bind
# but never delivers connections, so Expo Go could not reach the bundler.
#
# This host also has several IPv4 addresses (Ethernet, Wi-Fi, VirtualBox, WSL,
# link-local). Expo guesses one for the LAN URL and can pick an adapter the
# phone cannot route to. Pin it to the address on the phone's own subnet.
#
# Since Expo SDK 57 the CLI refuses to load this machine-personal variable from
# `.env`; put it in `apps/mobile/.env.local` (also gitignored) instead:
#
#   REACT_NATIVE_PACKAGER_HOSTNAME=192.168.1.12
#
# Use the SAME address for EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL above (with the API's port), and
# make sure Windows Firewall allows inbound node.exe on that adapter's profile.
